95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Anticipatory action \(AA\) enables humanitarian actors to act before crises escalate by linking forecasts and early warning systems with pre-arranged financing and early interventions that protect lives, livelihoods, and food security. Evidence from multiple countries has demonstrated the effectiveness of AA, while also highlighting the challenges of evaluating its impact in fragile and crisis-affected contexts. As AA expands and resources remain constrained, there is increasing demand for rigorous evidence on effectiveness, efficiency, prediction accuracy, and cost-effectiveness to inform program design, guide donor investments, and scale approaches where they work best. This workshop brings together practitioners, researchers, evaluators, Members, and partners to strengthen anticipatory action through improved analytics, learning, and collaboration, and to explore innovations in technology and disaster risk financing that can help translate evidence into action at scale.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
